@packages/sigilc/turtle.sigil from SigilTurtleInput import { AssertionValidation, FixedOntology }
@packages/core/src/design-input.sigil from SigilDesignInput import { ResolvedDesignInput, PhysicalInventory }

component SigilComputedClaims {
  goal {
    Decide the design findings that follow from an external interpretation of
    authored prose, and hand the rest to a judge as closed questions over
    computed facts.
  }

  interface {
    CompiledGuidance {
      Publish the claim vocabulary, the seven contract roles, one worked example
      per role, and the refusal cases to the external interpreter. Guidance is
      compiled into the binary and released with it; an operator may write an
      editable copy to a named path outside the workspace under validation.
      Fingerprint the guidance text, the vocabulary and the laws as one runtime
      identity. Guidance changes what the interpreter is told and never what the
      tool accepts.
    }

    InterpretationRequest {
      Project one design source and its resolved closure into an interpretation
      directory. Carry each Facet's exact prose slice with the contract role its
      unit belongs to, taken from ResolvedDesignInput rather than inferred, and
      emit one pre-filled row per Facet identifying that Facet alone. Write an
      immutable binding over the export digest, the selected source, the guidance
      fingerprint and the vocabulary generation. The caller keeps the directory
      and produces claims independently.
    }

    ReturnedClaims {
      Accept interpreted claims as data-only egglog atoms under AssertionValidation
      discipline: bound bytes before parsing and atom count before validation,
      reject every rule, command, schedule and non-literal argument, and refuse the
      whole artifact rather than its valid portion. Relations and properties are
      closed over FixedOntology. Modality distinguishes required, permitted and
      assumed commitments. A reading row records a Facet the interpreter read and
      found no commitment in, or whose intent is unresolved. Mint every claim
      identity; refuse interpreter-declared Component and Tag identities and any
      entity outside the resolved closure.
    }

    SectionAwareClosure {
      Re-emit accepted facts from parsed values into a tool-authored program and
      fill each claim's contract role from the PhysicalInventory unit it derives
      from. Derive holding relations, reachability, delegation, contradictions,
      ownership conflicts and obligations under finite tool-owned laws, then
      inspect absence only after the closure stabilizes. Rationale contributes no
      commitment: a claim whose role is Decisions is retained and reported but
      raises no obligation and satisfies none.
    }

    ComputedFindings {
      Report contradictions, ownership conflicts and unmet obligations with the
      claims and the law that produced each one. Report a claim whose subject and
      object coincide as degenerate, and a claim naming an entity absent from its
      own Facet's resolved references, owning component and provider components as
      ungrounded; neither satisfies its unit. Name a declared role that yielded
      neither a claim nor a reading row, and attribute that gap to the
      interpretation. An unchanged export and an unchanged interpretation produce
      an identical report.
    }

    JudgmentContext {
      Emit one entry per unit in the design, including units the closure found
      nothing about. Carry derived facts, obligation state and the provenance of
      each derived conclusion, and for every unfilled obligation the promise that
      raised it and where that promise is stated. Propose simplification
      candidates without ruling on them. Carry the Facet prose an entry refers to,
      so a consumer needs no access to the sources.
    }

    ClaimsCommands {
      Offer preparation, ingestion and guidance extraction as a separate
      executable beside the compiler. Refuse a binding that does not match the
      supplied export or the running guidance fingerprint. Exit zero for pass and
      warning, one for a gate failure, two for usage and three for operational
      failure.
    }
  }

  constraints {
    ClaimsCommands {
      Launch no model, worker or task workflow. The external interpretation is an
      input the caller supplies and re-supplies, never a call this executable
      makes.
    }

    ReturnedClaims {
      Interpreted text is data and is never executed as a program. Accepting a
      claim establishes neither that it is true of its Facet nor that the
      interpretation was faithful. No file outside the compiled binary widens what
      is accepted.
    }

    SectionAwareClosure {
      Workers supply no laws and fill no tool-owned table. The compiler's stored
      projections, its world cache and the files its runtime identity fingerprints
      are read-only to this component; writing any of them would invalidate every
      stored world. Findings and stores live under a path this component owns.
    }

    CompiledGuidance {
      Guidance discovered in the workspace under validation is refused. The test is
      provenance, not location.
    }
  }

  cases {
    SectionAwareClosure {
      The same claim text raises an obligation from a Constraints Facet and none
      from a Decisions Facet. A permitted commitment raises no obligation where a
      required one does. A Facet in a declared role that yields only a reading row
      is interpreted, and one that yields nothing at all is a named gap.
    }

    ReturnedClaims {
      An artifact carrying one valid claim beside one rule declaration is refused
      whole. A claim relating a local Facet to a Tag imported from a source in the
      closure is accepted.
    }
  }
}
